HYPOTHESIS (thrust 9): thrust 8 falsified the discovery edge (CC glob('*') returns the complete file
inventory ≈ zakcode's survey listing → both discover a REQUIRED value 12/12). The remaining candidate
edge is zakcode's deterministic zero-cost CONTENT-FOLD of guide files (AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md/ZAK.md) into
the system prompt, which should raise ADHERENCE to an UNPROMPTED convention — one the task never
mentions and that the agent has no functional reason to hunt for. PREDICTION FORK: CC adheres
(proactively reads guide files) -> PARITY; CC does not -> ZAK>CC (the fold is the real lever).

SETUP: task "implement version_string(major,minor,patch)". An arbitrary convention lives ONLY in
AGENTS.md: version strings are `v<MAJOR>.<MINOR>` with the patch OMITTED — overriding the model's
strong full-semver default on two axes (v-prefix + drop patch). Prompt never mentions it; task is
solvable-but-wrong without consulting AGENTS.md; trivial to apply once known (a one-line format), so a
fail is an ADHERENCE miss, not a coding miss. 26 files, AGENTS.md at root (plainly visible — this is NOT
a discovery test). Model-fixed zds-qwen3.6-35b via pod, N=12 each. CC unaided (no --surf). zakcode
--no-pin temp0 (folds AGENTS.md). Raw: cc-qwen-12-agents-md-convention.json (zc-01:/root),
determinism-zakcode-pinOFF-temp0-12-agents-md-convention.json (zc-01:/opt/zak-code-bench/bench/results).

