═══ MECHANISM (from the CC run JSON) — the gap is CONSULTATION, not discovery ═══
  CC globbed the workspace in 11/12 runs (so it SAW AGENTS.md in the file listing — thrust 8's
  glob('*') ≈ survey-listing holds), but READ AGENTS.md in 0/12 runs. Every CC run read ONLY
  versioning.py (the target), implemented version_string trivially as full semver, and returned. CC
  treats a self-contained-looking task as complete without consulting the guide file it can see.
  zakcode FOLDS AGENTS.md CONTENT into the system prompt every run → the convention is unconditionally
  in context → 12/12 adherence, no exploration needed. So discovery-INVENTORY is EQUAL (both see the
  file); the gap is whether the loop CONSULTS + APPLIES an unprompted convention.

═══ CONCLUSION: the durable beyond-parity property, isolated ═══
  zakcode's deterministic guide-file content-fold makes a small model ADHERE (12/12) to an unprompted
  convention that Claude Code ignores entirely (0/12). This is exactly the "more deterministic + works
  on smaller models" lever: the fold puts the rule in context so the model does not have to REMEMBER to
  look. It is NOT discovery (thrust 8 bounded that away) and NOT coding skill (trivial application,
  solvability-controlled). It is unconditional, zero-cost SURFACING of guidance.

═══ NEXT: CLAUDE.md control cell (pins the mechanism) ═══
  Same task/convention, convention moved to CLAUDE.md instead of AGENTS.md. Claude Code AUTO-LOADS
  CLAUDE.md, so PREDICTION: CC adheres -> PARITY (12/12 vs 12/12). That control proves the AGENTS.md
