═══ THE PINNING OBSERVATION — both loops adhere by CONTENT-FOLDING; they differ only in the FOLD-SET ═══
  CC PASSED 12/12 on the CLAUDE.md variant WITHOUT a single Read of CLAUDE.md (0/12; AGENTS.md 0/12). Zero
  reads + 12/12 adherence leaves exactly one channel: `claude -p` auto-loads CLAUDE.md into the system prompt
  — the SAME mechanism as zakcode's guide-file fold. So:
     Claude Code 2.1.267 (headless -p) fold-set:   {CLAUDE.md}
     zakcode (AGENT_GUIDE_FILENAMES) fold-set:      {AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, ZAK.md}
  Thrust 9's CC 0/12 on AGENTS.md is therefore NOT a task artifact (the byte-identical verify passes 12/12
  here), NOT a coding gap (CC solves it trivially once the rule is in context), NOT a harness artifact (12c
  proves this harness delivers CC's auto-load: same `claude -p`, cwd=ws, no config-suppressing flag), and NOT
  a zakcode advantage on content CC also has. It is precisely: CC does not fold AGENTS.md.

═══ THE DEFENSIBLE CLAIM (thrust 9 + this control, together) ═══
  On repos that ship AGENTS.md guidance (the cross-tool guide-file standard), zakcode makes a 35B model ADHERE
  (12/12) to an unprompted convention that Claude Code as-ships ignores entirely (0/12), because the fold puts
  the rule in context so the model never has to REMEMBER to look. On CLAUDE.md-only repos it is parity (this
  control) — consistent with the 11-task matched cell (as-good-or-better everywhere, worse nowhere). 0/12 vs
  12/12 at N=12: Fisher exact p<1e-6 (unlike the N=6 06-family cells). LIMITS: one convention KIND so far
  (string formatting) — thrust 10 tests another; CC's fold-set is a version property (a later CC that folds
  AGENTS.md closes this cell — the principle survives, the instance would not); the interactive (non -p) CC
  fold-set is unmeasured.

